# Known directmates. Format: <fen4> ; dm <depth>
#
# Generated for this project by seeded random construction, then classified by
# the prover and confirmed independently with python-chess: each position mates
# at the depth stated and does NOT mate one ply shallower, so every label is
# exact rather than an upper bound.
#
# ORDERING MATTERS: the first entry must have depth >= 2. The certificate
# forgery tests mutate a defender branch of the first proof, and a mate-in-1
# certificate is a leaf with no branches to mutate.
#
# The two entries with an en-passant square are deliberate, and in both the
# en-passant capture is itself the mate: a FEN-validation bug class has been
# found in this engine before, and only a crafted position exposed it.
8/2Q5/R7/8/1k4K1/8/8/8 w - - ; dm 2
1R6/8/8/8/7k/4Q3/4K3/8 w - - ; dm 2
8/2k5/8/4K1R1/8/8/6Q1/8 w - - ; dm 3
8/8/4Q3/8/2NK4/8/2k5/8 w - - ; dm 3
6k1/4n2R/8/8/8/3R4/8/6K1 w - - ; dm 3
8/6K1/6R1/7R/8/8/3k4/8 w - - ; dm 4
7k/5nN1/8/K7/1Q6/8/8/8 w - - ; dm 4
8/R3K3/8/6R1/8/2k5/8/8 w - - ; dm 5
6k1/8/8/8/8/5K2/5Q1N/8 w - - ; dm 5
8/4R3/8/1K6/8/8/2R5/k7 w - - ; dm 1
2Q5/k3K3/8/1pP5/8/8/8/1R6 w - b6 ; dm 1
7k/5K2/8/6pP/8/2R5/7Q/8 w - g6 ; dm 1
